<!-- Status bar icon. Android throws the colour away and keeps only the
     silhouette, so this is solid white on purpose: an icon with a gradient or
     with colour renders as a white square on the phone.

     It is a drawing, not a traced logo. The launcher mark is a photographic
     araguaney in bloom, and reducing that file to one ink gives a speckled
     blob at 24dp — the same reason `pubspec.yaml` declines to ship it as the
     monochrome layer of the adaptive icon. What survives at this size is the
     tree's outline: a broad lobed crown over a trunk that flares at the base.
     The crown is seven overlapping circles so the lobes stay visible once the
     system antialiases it down.

     Geometry sits inside the 20dp live area of the 24dp canvas (x 2..22,
     y 3.7..20.3). Crown and trunk are separate paths on purpose: merged into
     one, the trunk's winding would cancel against the circles and punch a hole
     through the middle. -->
